---
description: Vitest conventions for the Next.js frontend
globs: frontend/**/*.{test,spec}.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Frontend tests

- Use Vitest. Do not add Jest.
- Import `expect`, `test`, and `describe` from `vitest`. Do not rely on globals.
- Test synchronous Server and Client Components with Testing Library.
- Do not unit-test async Server Components in Vitest. Cover those with later E2E tests.
- Keep config in `frontend/vitest.config.mts`. Do not add a `vite.config` for the Next.js app.
- Do not assert fabricated business metrics. Test UI structure and real backend contracts only.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
import { render, screen } from "@testing-library/react";
import { expect, test } from "vitest";

test("renders the product heading", () => {
  render(<Page />);
  expect(
    screen.getByRole("heading", { name: "Jev Location Intelligence" }),
  ).toBeDefined();
});
```
